Falsifies `system_tests::user::non_volatile_memory_express_tests::a_confined_el0_server_cannot_dma_outside_its_region`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The confinement is skipped for the escape frame. The DMA-escape wiring (milestone 261 (the NVMe driver leaves the kernel)) stores the victim's physical base into
`non_volatile_memory_express::ESCAPE_TARGET`, which `find_and_confine` reads and adds to the NVMe
controller's IOMMU domain. The controller is then confined to a domain that *includes* the frame the
EL0 server aims its PRP at, so the out-of-region DMA lands instead of faulting: this is the
equivalent of skipping `iommu::confine` the test exists to catch (milestone 16b (IOMMU-backed driver isolation)), done precisely enough to widen the domain by exactly the one frame
rather than breaking the controller's own queues. (VT-d and both other units are default-deny, so
dropping confine outright would fault every admin DMA and the controller would never come up, which
is why the falsification widens rather than removes.)

The honest server, the geometry and the serve loop are untouched; the only change is which frames
the kernel tells the IOMMU the controller may reach, which is the whole of the confinement claim
(milestone 202 (every confinement test is a ritual until somebody breaks the confinement and watches it fail)).

Expected to fail: the `fault.unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(...))` in the test. With the victim frame
inside the domain the READ escape (disk -> victim) completes, so the IOMMU records no fault and the
bounded poll finds none. The `esc.is_canary_intact()` assertion also flips, because that completed READ
copies the disk image's zero bytes over the canary; either failure is the escape landing.
diff --git a/kernel/src/user/non_volatile_memory_express_service.rs b/kernel/src/user/non_volatile_memory_express_service.rs
--- a/kernel/src/user/non_volatile_memory_express_service.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/user/non_volatile_memory_express_service.rs
@@ -428,6 +428,8 @@
     // zero, so `victim` is not in the controller's domain and the escape below faults. The
     // replayable falsification inserts a store of `victim` into `ESCAPE_TARGET` right here, which
     // widens the domain to cover it; that one line is the whole patch.
+    crate::non_volatile_memory_express::ESCAPE_TARGET
+        .store(victim, core::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed);
     let found = crate::non_volatile_memory_express::find_and_confine().ok()?;
     let rid = found.rid;
     let scope = crate::iommu::scope_of(rid);
